<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ yr profit falls to NZ$225.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Air NZ yr profit falls to NZ$225.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 225.2 vs 260.2</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 50.8 vs 58.7</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				 12.0 vs 12.0</p>
<p>    Total div for yr (cents)		20.0 vs 20.0</p>
<p>    Turnover (billion)			 3.0 vs 2.9</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			   253.89 vs 286.19</p>
<p>    Tax					  25.08 vs 25.46</p>
<p>    Equity earnings		    loss 3.86 vs 1.68 profit</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 288.3 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date Nov 8</p>
<p>Reg date Oct 25</p>
<p>Ex div   Oct 29</p>
<p>Note - Air New Zealand is 19.9 percent owned by Qantas Airways and 42.5 percent by Brierley Investments Ltd.</p>
<p>Balance sheet (in millions unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current assets (billion)		1.18 vs 1.08</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion)		  3.13 vs 3.11</p>
<p>    Current liabilities		    957.3 vs 822.55</p>
<p>    Total liabilities  (billion)	  1.73 vs 1.83</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity (billion)	1.40 vs 1.28</p>
<p>Cashflow from operating activities 425.8 vs 412.9</p>
<p>Cashflow from investing activities(142.1)vs (371.3)</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
